; `Bool` is the one non-data column the exhaustiveness matrix can
; enumerate: `true` and `false` are two nullary constructors as far
; as coverage goes. Until 2026-08-21 only the top-level
; `armsBoolComplete` special case knew it, so a `Bool` nested in a
; constructor was coverable by nothing but a binder, and the complete
; `full` below was AX3005 "some values are not covered".
;
;   line 15: `(Some true)` with no `(Some false)`   AX3005, missing false
;
; `full` emits nothing: both literals and `None` are present.
(:: full (-> (Option Bool) Int))

(fn (full o)
  (match o
    ((Some true) 1)
    ((Some false) 2)
    ((None) 0)
  )
)

(:: half (-> (Option Bool) Int))

(fn (half o)
  (match o
    ((Some true) 1)
    ((None) 0)
  )
)

(:: main Int)

(fn (main) 0)
